date-released: "2026-09-25"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22950553"
# Concept DOI (all versions): 10.5281/zenodo.22950552
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked formalizations of arguments in the Śūraṅgama Sūtra
  (Taishō T19 no. 945) in Lean 4. Premises are structure fields rather than
  global axioms; every positive result is paired with a finite countermodel
  that shows which premise carries it; axiom-dependency reports are recorded.
  Version 0.1.0 covers the seven-location argument (七處徵心) under an
  explicitly named reading. The project does not assert the truth of a
  doctrine or a uniquely correct reading. Development was AI-assisted
  (Claude, Anthropic) under human direction; proof acceptance is determined
  by the Lean kernel, and source selection, readings, and claim boundaries
  are the author's responsibility.
